<title>USA: San Antonio feeder cattle prices steady-firm - USDA.</title>
<headline>San Antonio feeder cattle prices steady-firm - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers were steady to firm, compared to Monday, USDA said.</p>
<p>Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 300-600 lb feeder steers and heifers. Supply included around 3 percent slaughter cows and bulls; 21 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs with balance mostly feeder cattle under 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>70.25-82.25; 700-800 lbs 68.00-73.00; few 800-850 lbs</p>
<p>70.50-77.00. Medium and Large 1-2 - few 200-275 lbs</p>
<p>89.00-91.00; 300-400 lbs 80.25- 87.00; 400-500 lbs</p>
<p>75.25-82.50; 500-575 lbs 72.50-74.25. Large 2 Holsteins - two pkgs 375-475 lbs 55.50-57.00.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-705 lbs</p>
<p>69.00-72.00, pkg replacement quality 80.50; 700-750 lbs</p>
<p>65.50-68.50; pkg 840 lbs 64.50.</p>
<p>Receipts - 346    Last Week - 411    Last Year - 812</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
